{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011KfGZbLb2aaHZKmTnYMofR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements 111 GNU coreutils/moreutils utilities in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test specification-driven code generation via the mage-claude-orchestrator pipeline.\n\n**Architecture**: `cmd/<name>/` per utility, `pkg/testutils/` (diff testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/hashutil/` (shared hash operations), `pkg/sizeparse/` (size parsing), `pkg/encutil/` (shared encoding/decoding). Specs in `docs/specs/`.\n\n**Current state**: All 33 releases (00.0-15.0) are spec_complete. Only `pkg/sys` and `pkg/sizeparse` have code implemented. All other packages and all 111 cmd/ utilities have code status \"not started.\" All requirements in `requirement_states` are \"ready.\"\n\n**Current release**: 00.0 (foundational infrastructure). Remaining use cases: uc001-magefiles, uc002-format, uc004-testutils, uc005-hashutil, uc007-encutil.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 00.0 has five incomplete use cases. However, `srd001-testutils` and `srd003-format` have **no entries in requirement_states**, so I cannot propose tasks for them (constraint: \"only propose tasks for R-items with status 'ready'\"). Two packages DO have ready requirements:\n\n- **srd088-encutil** (8 reqs, all ready) -- enables base32, base64, basenc\n- **srd086-hashutil** (9 reqs, all ready) -- enables md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum, sha224sum, sha384sum, b2sum, cksum, sum\n\nBoth are independent libraries in release 00.0. Alphabetical ordering: encutil before hashutil. Contracts before implementations.\n\n## Weight Budget Checks\n\nAssuming default weight 1 per requirement (cannot read requirements.yaml per no-tools constraint):\n\n**Task 0**: encutil contract -- no SRD