o (EncoderConfig, Encode) and decode.go (DecoderConfig, Decode, OpenInput) following Go convention of one file per logical concern\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/encutil/... succeeds with no errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/encutil/... reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"All five exported symbols (EncoderConfig, DecoderConfig, Encode, Decode, OpenInput) are present with correct signatures\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"No imports of cmd/ or other pkg/ packages\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"pkg/hashutil contract (srd086-hashutil)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd086-hashutil.yaml (hash utility library SRD -- defines all requirements, types, and function signatures)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/ component descriptions, import constraints, and design decisions)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/hashutil/hashconfig.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"HashConfig, CheckOptions types and FormatGNU, FormatBSDTag, ComputeDigest, ParseChecksumLine, VerifyChecksums, DigestFiles function stubs\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define HashConfig struct with fields: Algorithm string, NewHash func() hash.Hash, DigestLen int\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Define CheckOptions struct with fields: Warn bool, Quiet bool, Status bool\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Define FormatGNU signature: func(digest, filename string, binary bool) string -- panic stub\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Define FormatBSDTag signature: func(algorithm, filename, digest string) string -- panic stub\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Define ComputeDigest signature: func(r io.Reader, cfg HashConfig) (string, error) -- panic stub\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Define ParseChecksumLine signature: func(line string, cfg HashConfig) (filename, expectedDigest string, binary bool, err error) -- panic stub\"\n      - id: R7\n        text: \"Define VerifyChecksums signature: func(checksumFile string, cfg HashConfig, opts CheckOptions, stdout, stderr io.Writer) (bool, error) -- panic stub\"\n      - id: R8\n        text: \"Define DigestFiles signature: func(files []string, cfg HashConfig, binary, tag bool, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int -- panic stub\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"All function bodies are panic(\\\"not implemented\\\") stubs -- implementation follows in separate tasks\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Import constraints per ARCHITECTURE: must not import any cmd/ package or any other pkg/ package\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Primary file named hashconfig.go after the primary exported type HashConfig (pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go is forbidden per P7)\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/hashutil/... succeeds with no errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/hashutil/... reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"All eight exported symbols (HashConfig, CheckOptions, FormatGNU, FormatBSDTag, ComputeDigest, ParseChecksumLine, VerifyChecksums, DigestFiles) present with correct signatures\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"No imports of cmd/ or other pkg/ packages\"\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"pkg/encutil encoding implementation (srd088-encutil R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd088-encutil.yaml (read requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1 for exact specification and acceptance criteria)\n      - pkg/encutil/encode.go (contract stubs from task 0 -- replace Encode panic stub with implementation)\n      - pkg/encutil/decode.go (contract stubs from task 0 -- reference DecoderConfig type)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/encutil/encode.go\n        action: modify\n        note: \"Replace Encode panic stub with full implementation including line wrapping at WrapCol\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd088-encutil R1.1 per SRD -- EncoderConfig usage in the encoding pipeline\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd088-encutil R1.2 per SRD -- Encode reads all input from io.Reader, applies cfg.Encode to produce encoded output\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd088-encutil R1.3 per SRD -- line wrapping splits encoded output into lines of cfg.WrapCol characters\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd088-encutil R2.1 per SRD -- DecoderConfig type fully defined with Decode function field and IgnoreGarbage flag\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Import constraints per ARCHITECTURE: must not import any cmd/ package or any other pkg/ package\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow the exact type signatures defined in the srd088-encutil contract\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/encutil/... succeeds\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/encutil/... reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Encode function reads from io.Reader, applies cfg.Encode, wraps output at cfg.WrapCol columns, writes to io.Writer\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"All SRD acceptance criteria for R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1 are satisfied\"\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"pkg/encutil decoding and input handling (srd088-encutil R2.2, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd088-encutil.yaml (read requirements R2.2, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2 for exact specification and acceptance criteria)\n      - pkg/encutil/decode.go (contract stubs from task 0 -- replace Decode and OpenInput panic stubs with implementations)\n      - pkg/encutil/encode.go (reference for consistent style and patterns from task 2)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/encutil/decode.go\n        action: modify\n        note: \"Replace Decode and OpenInput panic stubs with full implementations\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd088-encutil R2.2 per SRD -- Decode reads encoded input, strips whitespace, decodes via cfg.Decode, writes to io.Writer\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd088-encutil R2.3 per SRD -- IgnoreGarbage handling during decode (skip non-alphabet characters when true, error when false)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd088-encutil R3.1 per SRD -- OpenInput returns os.Stdin for \\\"-\\\" filename, opens and returns named file otherwise\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd088-encutil R3.2 per SRD -- error handling and propagation for IO and decode errors\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Import constraints per ARCHITECTURE: must not import any cmd/ package or any other pkg/ package\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow the exact type signatures defined in the srd088-encutil contract\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/encutil/... succeeds\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/encutil/... reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Decode function reads from io.Reader, handles garbage per IgnoreGarbage flag, decodes via cfg.Decode, writes to io.Writer\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"OpenInput returns os.Stdin when filename is \\\"-\\\" and opens the named file otherwise\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"All SRD acceptance criteria for R2.2, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2 are satisfied\"\n```\n\n**Note**: srd001-testutils and srd003-format have no entries in `requirement_states`, so no tasks are proposed for them despite their use cases being incomplete in release 00.0. Next batch should cover srd086-hashutil implementation (R1.1-R3.2, 9 requirements across 3 tasks) and encutil tests."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60989,"cach